  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Let's define a function F(X)F(X)F(X) as follows:\n\nF(X)=XYF(X) = \\frac{X}{Y}F(X)=YX​\n\nwhere YYY is the largest perfect square that divides XXX.\n\nFor example,\n\n\nThe largest perfect square that divides 121212 is 444. Hence F(12)=124=3F(12) =  \\frac{12}{4} = 3F(12)=412​=3.\nThe largest perfect square that divides 363636 is 363636. Hence F(36)=3636=1F(36) =  \\frac{36}{36} = 1F(36)=3636​=1.\nThe largest perfect square that divides 777 is 111. Hence F(7)=71=7F(7) =  \\frac{7}{1} = 7F(7)=17​=7.\nYou are given an array AAA consisting of NNN integers. A pair of integer (iii, jjj) is called Good if 1≤i&lt;j≤N1 \\leq i \\lt j \\leq N1≤i&lt;j≤N and  F(Ai∗Aj)&gt;1F(A_i * A_j) \\gt 1F(Ai​∗Aj​)&gt;1. Find the number of Good pairs.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains an integer NNN.\nThe second line of each testcase contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\dots , A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, print a single line containing one integer - the number of Good pairs.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\leq T \\leq 10^41≤T≤104",
      "1≤N≤1051 \\leq N \\leq 10^51≤N≤105",
      "1≤Ai≤1061 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^61≤Ai​≤106",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 10610^6106."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n3\n2 3 12\n4 \n1 2 3 4\n3\n2 3 7",
        "output": "2\n5\n3",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111:\n\n(i=1,j=2)(i = 1, j = 2)(i=1,j=2): F(A1∗A2)=F(2∗3)=F(6)=61=6>1F(A_1 * A_2) = F(2 * 3) = F(6) = \\frac{6}{1} = 6 \\gt 1F(A1​∗A2​)=F(2∗3)=F(6)=16​=6>1.\n(i=1,j=3)(i = 1, j = 3)(i=1,j=3): F(A1∗A3)=F(2∗12)=F(24)=244=6>1F(A_1 * A_3) = F(2 *12) = F(24) = \\frac{24}{4} = 6 \\gt 1F(A1​∗A3​)=F(2∗12)=F(24)=424​=6>1.\n(i=2,j=3)(i = 2, j = 3)(i=2,j=3): F(A2∗A3)=F(3∗12)=F(36)=3636=1≯1F(A_2 * A_3) = F(3 *12) = F(36) = \\frac{36}{36} = 1 \\ngtr 1F(A2​∗A3​)=F(3∗12)=F(36)=3636​=1≯1.\n\nSo there are 2 Good pairs.\nTest case 222:  All pairs except (1,41, 41,4) are Good pairs as F(A1∗A4)=F(1∗4)=F(4)=44=1≯1F(A_1 * A_4) = F(1 * 4) = F(4) = \\frac{4}{4} = 1 \\ngtr 1F(A1​∗A4​)=F(1∗4)=F(4)=44​=1≯1.\nTest case 333:  All pairs are Good pairs."
      }
